{
  "name": "NSE F&O: a future and an option, and everything this venue refuses",
  "protocol": "nnf",
  "dialect": "nsefo",
  "fix_port": 9031,
  "control_port": 9104,
  "server_comp_id": "NSEFO-SIM",
  "sessions": {
    "one": {
      "comp_id": "50521",
      "protocol": "nnf"
    },
    "two": {
      "comp_id": "50777",
      "protocol": "nnf"
    }
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "comment": "F&O is a separate trading system from Capital Market -- its own gateway on 9031, its own boxes and its own users -- so nothing here touches the cash venue on 9021. Tags are F&O's own numbering, which is deliberately not Capital Market's: 9402=UserId, 9403=ErrorCode, 9650=BoxId, 9459=BrokerId, 9530/9531=sign-on user and password, 55/9410/9411/9412/9413=the five CONTRACT_DESC fields, 9449=BookType, 54=BuySell, 38=Volume, 44=Price, 37=OrderNumber, 9462=Pro/Client, 9624=Day, 9627=AON, 9622=StopLoss."
    },
    {
      "control": "state.set",
      "args": {
        "market": "NORMAL",
        "state": "OPEN"
      }
    },
    {
      "control": "orders.cancel_all",
      "args": {
        "market": "NORMAL"
      }
    },
    {
      "control": "stats.reset",
      "args": {
        "market": "NORMAL",
        "symbol": "NIFTY-FUTIDX-24SEP2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Box 101, broker 10123, user 50521. Registration, box sign-on, then the user over it -- the same three-step sequence Capital Market has, because the box/user session model is the protocol's, not the segment's."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "23008",
        "9403": "0",
        "9650": "101"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "23009",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "23000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9650": "101",
        "9459": "10123"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "23001",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2300",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "9530": "50521",
        "9531": "Nse@2026",
        "9459": "10123"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2301",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Box 102, broker 10456, user 50777."
    },
    {
      "send": "two",
      "fields": {
        "35": "23008",
        "9403": "0",
        "9650": "102"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "two",
      "fields": {
        "35": "23009",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "send": "two",
      "fields": {
        "35": "23000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9650": "102",
        "9459": "10456"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "two",
      "fields": {
        "35": "23001",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "send": "two",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2300",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50777",
        "9530": "50777",
        "9531": "Nse@2026",
        "9459": "10456"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "two",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2301",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "clear": "one"
    },
    {
      "clear": "two"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A NIFTY future. The expiry travels as seconds from 1 Jan 1980, and a future's StrikePrice is -1 rather than 0 -- the protocol breaking its own 'zero means absent' rule, which is why it is asserted here. The lot is 25, so the quantity is a multiple of it."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "50",
        "44": "25400.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "1": "CLIENT001",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9624": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2073",
        "9403": "0",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9412": "-1",
        "38": "50",
        "151": "50",
        "14": "0",
        "44": "25400.00"
      },
      "capture": {
        "future": "37"
      }
    },
    {
      "control": "bbo",
      "args": {
        "market": "NORMAL",
        "symbol": "NIFTY-FUTIDX-24SEP2026"
      },
      "expect_result": {
        "bid": "25400.00",
        "bid_qty": 50,
        "ask": null
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "The other member sells 25 into it. Both sides get a trade confirmation with their own running totals, and the resting side's arrives on the other box."
    },
    {
      "send": "two",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50777",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "2",
        "38": "25",
        "44": "25400.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "1": "CLIENT777",
        "9459": "10456",
        "9624": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "two",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2222",
        "32": "25",
        "31": "25400.00",
        "14": "25"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2222",
        "32": "25",
        "31": "25400.00",
        "151": "25",
        "14": "25"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Amend the remainder by the exchange's own order number -- there is no client order ID in this protocol either."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2040",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "37": "$future",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "50",
        "44": "25350.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9624": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2074",
        "9403": "0",
        "37": "$future",
        "44": "25350.00"
      }
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2070",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "37": "$future",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "50",
        "44": "25350.00",
        "9459": "10123"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2075",
        "9403": "0",
        "37": "$future"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "An option on the same underlying: the strike is real and the option type is CE, where the future carried -1 and XX."
    },
    {
      "clear": "one"
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "OPTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "25000.00",
        "9413": "CE",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "25",
        "44": "420.50",
        "9462": "1",
        "1": "CLIENT001",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9624": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2073",
        "9403": "0",
        "9410": "OPTIDX",
        "9413": "CE",
        "151": "25"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Book 3 is Stop Loss and Market-If-Touched together -- a conflation Capital Market does not have -- and neither is built, so the book itself is refused with e$invalid_book_type."
    },
    {
      "clear": "one"
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "3",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "25",
        "44": "25400.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9624": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2231",
        "9403": "16406"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "The SL bit on a Regular Lot order names the order type rather than the book, so it gets its own code, SL_NOT_ALLOWED."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "25",
        "44": "25400.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9622": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2231",
        "9403": "16445"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "All Or None: 16319."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "25",
        "44": "25400.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9624": "Y",
        "9627": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2231",
        "9403": "16319"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "A quantity that is not a multiple of the contract's lot -- 20 against NIFTY's 25. Lot size is per contract here, not per venue."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "20",
        "44": "25400.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9624": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2231",
        "9403": "16328"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Outside the contract's own circuit filter: 16284."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "25",
        "44": "99999.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9624": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2231",
        "9403": "16284"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "A contract that is not listed: 16012."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "55": "NOSUCH",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "25",
        "44": "100.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9624": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2231",
        "9403": "16012"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Message recovery, the only thing this protocol has where FIX has a ResendRequest. 7000 names a stream in the header's AlphaChar and a cursor in SequenceNumber (9492); the answer is HEADER_RECORD (7011), a MESSAGE_RECORD (7021) per message after that cursor, and TRAILER_RECORD (7031). 9405 is the header's TimeStamp1, which IS that cursor -- so the download resumes from a value the venue assigned, which is why this captures it rather than hard-coding one. Without that, the scenario would replay the whole daemon's history on its second run in the same process and assert against a moving target."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "1600",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "1601",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521"
      },
      "capture": {
        "cursor": "9405"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Nothing has happened since that system information, so the download is a header and a trailer with no records between them. A client that is up to date still asks on every reconnection and must be told 'nothing' rather than handed its whole day again."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "9492": "$cursor"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7011",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7031",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Now give it something to recover: an order that rests, and then the same download again. The confirmation comes back inside a MESSAGE_RECORD -- and the record's own header is the ordinary MESSAGE_HEADER, which is what lets the decoder on this side read the transaction code at offset 0 of the payload at all."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "55": "NIFTY",
        "9410": "FUTIDX",
        "9411": "1474675200",
        "9412": "-1",
        "9413": "XX",
        "9449": "1",
        "54": "1",
        "38": "50",
        "44": "25400.00",
        "9462": "1",
        "1": "CLIENT001",
        "9459": "10123",
        "9624": "Y"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "2073",
        "9403": "0"
      },
      "capture": {
        "recovered": "37"
      }
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "9492": "$cursor"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7011",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7021",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7031",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "A stream this venue does not serve is empty rather than an error: a member loops the download over every stream the system information advertised, and refusing one would stop that loop. AlphaChar carries the stream as a BYTE, not a digit -- 9401 here is chr(99)."
    },
    {
      "send": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7000",
        "9403": "0",
        "9402": "50521",
        "9401": "c",
        "9492": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7011",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "expect": "one",
      "fields": {
        "35": "7031",
        "9403": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "control": "orders.cancel_all",
      "args": {
        "market": "NORMAL"
      }
    },
    {
      "control": "state.set",
      "args": {
        "market": "NORMAL",
        "state": "CLOSED"
      }
    }
  ]
}
